rough them in frames 25–28.\n\n---\n\n**6. Exiting station to outside:**\n✅ **Confirmed.** Frame 29 shows the exterior of the station, with open sky, trees, buildings, and people walking outside. This is the final frame in the sequence and confirms they have exited the station.\n\n---\n\n### **Summary of Sequence and Missing Elements:**\n\n**Complete Sequence Observed:**\n1. **Frames 1–14:** Both vloggers are together, ascending stairs/escalator (Frame 1), then walking through a station concourse (Frames 2–14). They are not seen exiting a train or on a platform with tracks.\n2. **Frames 15–18:** The camera switches to a third-person view, showing a corridor leading toward the exit gates.\n3. **Frames 19–28:** The vloggers (though not individually visible) are implied to pass through the turnstile gates, as people are seen doing so.\n4. **Frame 29:** The exterior of the station is shown, confirming they have exited.\n\n**Missing or Unclear Actions:**\n- **Exiting train doors:** Not shown.\n- **Train platform with visible tracks:** Not shown.\n- **Individual visibility during turnstile passage:** The vloggers are not individually visible in frames 19–28, so it is not confirmed they passed through the turnstiles *in frame*, though it is strongly implied by context.\n\n---\n\n### **Conclusion:**\nThe sequence of events from the provided frames shows the two vloggers ascending stairs/escalator, walking through a station concourse, and exiting through turnstiles to the outside. However, the initial steps — exiting the train and being on a platform with visible tracks — are **not captured** in the provided frames. The video begins *after* they have left the train, and the station platform with tracks is never shown. The turnstile passage is implied but not visually confirmed for the vloggers themselves.\n\nThis suggests the provided frames capture only a portion of the full journey from train to outside, missing the very beginning (train exit and platform) and the exact mo